        "surveyType": "Standard Survey",
        "narrative": "<p>Walleye were very abundant, and present in a wide range of sizes, with most between 12 and 18 inches.  There appeared to be good natural reproduction in most years, and the population was entirely self-sustained.  Yellow perch were also very abundant and, with a mean weight of 0.9 lb/fish, were larger than usual for lakes in this area.  Northern pike and smallmouth bass were present in average numbers.  Most of the northern pike collected were small, two-year-old fish, while most of the smallmouth bass collected were relatively large (12-19 inches).</p>",
